  "notes": "{賛同|さんどう} expresses agreement or support for an idea, opinion, or cause. It is more formal than {賛成|さんせい} and often implies active endorsement rather than mere agreement.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {賛同|さんどう}を{得|え}る (gain support)\n- {賛同|さんどう}する (to endorse, agree with)\n- {賛同者|さんどうしゃ} (supporter, endorser)\n- Xに{賛同|さんどう}する (support X, agree with X)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {賛同|さんどう} vs {賛成|さんせい}: {賛同|さんどう} implies deeper alignment with a cause or idea and active support, while {賛成|さんせい} is a more general term for agreement or approval, often used in voting contexts.",
